<title>USA: General Electric deal gets Justice clearance.</title>
<headline>General Electric deal gets Justice clearance.</headline>
<dateline>EVENDALE, Ohio 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Co said Monday that the U.S. Department of Justice has cleared its acquisition of Greenwich Air Services Inc.</p>
<p>GE said it intends to complete the transaction on September 2.</p>
<p>GE is acquiring Greenwich through a combination of GE stock and cash valued at $530 million, or $31 per share of Greenwich stock.</p>
<p>Greenwich Air, based in Miami, Fla., is a diversified, independent jet engine maintenance and overhaul company.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
